Chapter: VmTouchRefusal
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A hand arm for codex-vm's commit refusals (DeviceEmulationCatalog.md, "A host
 commit that fails is a refusal"). The texture upload and the asset load are
 pointed at guest RAM no program touches on a default guest (0x60000000 and
 0x60400000, two separate 2 MB chunks), so the host commits each range itself.
 The asset path is this chapter under the -asset-root codex/test of its
 sidecar, written as ASCII bytes because the host opens it with fopen.

Section: Path

  path-bytes : List Integer = [118, 109, 45, 116, 111, 117, 99, 104, 45, 114, 101, 102, 117, 115, 97, 108, 46, 99, 111, 100, 101, 120]

  put-path : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  put-path (b) (i) =
    if i >= list-length path-bytes then poke-byte b i 0
    else let p = poke-byte b i (list-at path-bytes i) in put-path b (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Gpu.Compute] Nothing = act
    a <- gpu-out #408 #60000000
    b <- gpu-out #409 8
    c <- gpu-out #40A 8
    d <- gpu-out #40B 1
    let buf = alloc-bytes 64
    in let w = put-path buf 0
    in act
      e <- gpu-out #40C buf
      f <- gpu-out #40D #60400000
      g <- gpu-out #417 0
      n <- gpu-in #40E
      print-line-uni ("asset bytes " & show n)
      print-line-uni "survived"
    end
  end
